Understanding the Code and How Spring Reactive (Mono) is Used

This code is implementing feature flag handling for a system related to plans and offers (SFOs - Special Feature Offers) using Spring Reactive (Mono). It retrieves feature flags, processes them, and updates plans accordingly. Let’s go step by step:


---

1. Feature Flag Management Using Spring Reactive (Mono)

Fetching Feature Flags

File: FeatureFlagHelper.java

public Mono<Map<String, Boolean>> fetchFeatureFlags() {
    Map<String, Boolean> featureFlagsMap = new HashMap<>();
    
    Mono<Boolean> legacySfosFFlagMono = featureFlag.isFeatureEnabled(
        FeatureFlagConstants.AWS_CONFIG_APP_NAME,
        FeatureFlagConstants.SWIFT_CFG_PROFILE,
        FeatureFlagConstants.LEGACY_SFOS_FFLAG,
        false
    );

    return Mono.zip(
        fwaDuplicatePerkFFlagMono, 
        availableOffersCarouselFFlagMono, 
        promoBadgingFFlagMono, 
        unlimitedCloudPerkModalFFlagMono, 
        legacySfosFFlagMono
    ).flatMap(tuple -> {
        Boolean fwaDuplicatePerkFFlag = tuple.getT1();
        Boolean availableOffersCarouselFFlag = tuple.getT2();
        Boolean promoBadgingFFlag = tuple.getT3();
        Boolean unlimitedCloudPerkModalFFlag = tuple.getT4();
        Boolean legacySfosFFlag = tuple.getT5();

        featureFlagsMap.put(FeatureFlagConstants.FWA_DUPLICATE_PERK_FFLAG, fwaDuplicatePerkFFlag);
        featureFlagsMap.put(FeatureFlagConstants.AWS_FLAG_SPECIAL_OFFER, availableOffersCarouselFFlag);
        featureFlagsMap.put(FeatureFlagConstants.PROMO_BADGING_FFLAG, promoBadgingFFlag);
        featureFlagsMap.put(FeatureFlagConstants.UNLIMITED_CLOUD_PERK_MODEL_FFLAG, unlimitedCloudPerkModalFFlag);
        featureFlagsMap.put(FeatureFlagConstants.LEGACY_SFOS_FFLAG, legacySfosFFlag);

        log.info("featureFlagsMap: {}", featureFlagsMap);

        return Mono.just(featureFlagsMap);
    });
}

What’s Happening Here?

Mono<Boolean> legacySfosFFlagMono: Fetches a feature flag value asynchronously.

Mono.zip(...).flatMap(tuple -> { ... }):

Collects multiple feature flag values in parallel using Mono.zip().

Extracts flag values from tuple (e.g., tuple.getT1(), tuple.getT2(), etc.).

Populates the featureFlagsMap with the extracted values.

Returns the map wrapped in a Mono<Map<String, Boolean>>.



How Spring Reactive (Mono) is Used?

Mono.zip(): Aggregates multiple Mono<Boolean> values into a single Mono<Tuple>.

flatMap(): Extracts values, updates featureFlagsMap, and returns a reactive Mono<Map<String, Boolean>>.

Asynchronous execution: This allows non-blocking retrieval of feature flags.



