2. Assisted Plan Service - Processing Feature Flags

File: AssistedPlanServiceImpl.java

public class AssistedPlanServiceImpl implements AssistedPlanService {
    if (CollectionUtilities.isNotEmptyOrNull(availablePlanMobileInfo)) {
        soeLine.setProfilePerks(planServiceHelper.setProfilePerks(
            availablePlanMobileInfo.get(0).getCurrentSPOs(),
            soeData.getPerkReferenceDataList()
        ));

        if (CollectionUtilities.isNotEmptyOrNull(getPlansRequest.getFeatureFlags()) &&
            getPlansRequest.getFeatureFlags().containsKey(FeatureFlagConstants.LEGACY_SFOS_FFLAG) &&
            getPlansRequest.getFeatureFlags().get(FeatureFlagConstants.LEGACY_SFOS_FFLAG)) {
            
            String legacySfo = env.getProperty(PlanConstants.LEGACY_SFOS);
            
            PlanServiceCommonHelper.setLegacySfos(soeLine, availablePlanMobileInfo, legacySfo);
        }
    }
}

What’s Happening Here?

1. Checking if availablePlanMobileInfo is not empty.

This ensures the data is available before proceeding.



2. Setting Profile Perks using planServiceHelper.setProfilePerks(...).


3. Checking Feature Flags from Request:

If LEGACY_SFOS_FFLAG exists and is true, it proceeds with setLegacySfos().

Reads legacy_sfos from application.properties (PlanConstants.LEGACY_SFOS).

Calls setLegacySfos(...) to update SOE (Service Offer Entity).





