3. Utility Class for Feature Flags

File: PlanServiceCommonHelper.java

public static void setFeatureFlagsToSOE(GetPlansRequest getPlansRequest, GetPlansData getPlansData) {
    Map<String, Boolean> featureFlags = 
        CollectionUtilities.isNotEmptyOrNull(getPlansRequest.getFeatureFlags()) 
            ? getPlansRequest.getFeatureFlags() 
            : new HashMap<>();

    if (featureFlags.containsKey(FeatureFlagConstants.LEGACY_SFOS_FFLAG)) {
        setFeatureFlagsToSOE(
            FeatureFlagConstants.LEGACY_SFOS_FFLAG, 
            featureFlags.get(FeatureFlagConstants.LEGACY_SFOS_FFLAG), 
            getPlansData
        );
    }
}

What’s Happening Here?

1. Extracts feature flags from getPlansRequest safely.


2. Checks if LEGACY_SFOS_FFLAG exists in the feature flags.


3. Calls setFeatureFlagsToSOE(...) to apply it to getPlansData.




