Summary of What’s Happening in the Code

Main Purpose

This implementation adds handling for the "legacySfos" feature flag, which determines whether a legacy Special Feature Offer (SFO) should be applied.


Spring Reactive (Mono) Usage

Mono<Boolean> is used to fetch feature flags asynchronously.

Mono.zip() collects multiple flags in parallel.

flatMap() processes the flags and stores them in a Map<String, Boolean>.


Feature Flag Flow

1. Feature Flags are fetched asynchronously (FeatureFlagHelper.fetchFeatureFlags()).


2. Flags are passed to AssistedPlanServiceImpl to decide whether to apply LEGACY_SFOS_FFLAG.


3. If enabled, the system applies legacy SFO changes (PlanServiceCommonHelper.setLegacySfos()).



Why Spring Reactive?

Non-blocking execution: Fetching feature flags doesn't block the main thread.

Performance improvement: Parallel fetching of multiple feature flags.

Scalability: Works well in microservices architecture.



