How to Apply This Knowledge to Other Projects?

When adding a new feature flag:

1. Define it in FeatureFlagConstants.


2. Fetch it using a Mono<Boolean> in a helper class.


3. Process it using Mono.zip() if multiple flags are needed together.


4. Use it in services to modify business logic.


5. Ensure it is safely checked before applying changes.



When working with Spring Reactive (Mono):

Use Mono for single values (e.g., Mono<Boolean>).

Use Mono.zip() when combining multiple Mono values.

Always use flatMap() for processing values reactively.




